  "verbalization": "Certolizumab Pegol, a monoclonal antibody targeting tumor necrosis factor (TNF), is implicated in the treatment of inflammatory conditions such as Ankylosing Spondylitis. The evidence suggests that Certolizumab Pegol may be associated with Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD) through a chain of indications involving Ankylosing Spondylitis and its treatment with corticosteroids. This pathway highlights a potential mechanistic link where TNF inhibition, a core function of Certolizumab Pegol, could influence the inflammatory processes that underlie IBD. The presence of multiple indirect pathways—each linking Certolizumab Pegol to Ankylosing Spondylitis and then to IBD—supports the hypothesis that the drug may exert a modulatory effect on inflammatory pathways in IBD. The evidence is consistent with a role in reducing inflammation, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of corticosteroid use in the management of IBD, and suggests that Certolizumab Pegol may offer a novel therapeutic approach by targeting the underlying inflammatory drivers.",
